\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two branches form a closed curve}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In the SNLC column of \ref{fnip-0086}, a current between the
folds gives three equilibria. Only the lower one is stable.
\citet{Figure 3.5, p. 59}{ermentrout2010mathematical} draws the
unstable manifold of the [saddle](fnip-0035). Its two branches meet the
stable [node](fnip-0035), and the union of those branches is a closed
curve. As the current increases, the node and the saddle meet at the
fold that \citet{Figure 3.6a, p. 60}{ermentrout2010mathematical}
labels #{\mathrm{SN}_{2}}.
Past that fold the closed curve is a stable periodic orbit.
\citet{p. 59}{ermentrout2010mathematical} records that stability.
The frequency of the orbit can be arbitrarily low.
\citet{§6.1.2, p. 164}{izhikevich2007dynamical} describes the same
curve and the periodic orbit that remains after those two equilibria
meet.}
